# REQUIRES: llvm-as, llvm-dis, opt, llvm-17.0.6
#
# NF-A02 -- CLOSED SCALAR ARITHMETIC SURFACE (preflight seed).
#
# Before this test the whole harness contained zero floating-point IR:
#   grep -rEn '\b(fadd|fmul|fsub|fdiv|fcmp|fneg|fptrunc|fpext|sitofp|uitofp)\b'
# returned nothing. NF-A02 and Lemma R5.0N are entirely about which FP opcodes
# may appear, so there was no witness of any kind for either side of the line.
#
# WHAT THE PROFILE ACTUALLY SAYS (NF-A02, section 15). The module contains
# flag-free modulo integer arithmetic and checked division and shift operands.
# "Floating-point values occur only in bit-preserving movement, same-width
# bitcasts, `fneg`, and `fcmp`; the frozen closure contains no FP arithmetic,
# width conversion, or FP/integer numeric conversion."
#
# Metatheory Lemma R5.0N supplies the reason and the two lists:
# NoAmbiguousNaNResult_e(T) holds exactly when the frozen closure contains no
# FP arithmetic, FP-width conversion, or FP/integer numeric conversion; any
# residual such opcode yields Unknown(PONFFPArithmeticUnsupported) "before
# relational construction, even if it is dynamically unreachable, its actual
# arguments would produce a non-NaN result, or a target claim selects one
# result". The admitted side is: "Loads, stores, same-width bitcasts, phi,
# select, and `fneg` preserve exact input bits, while `fcmp` produces the fixed
# predicate-defined Boolean".
#
# So `fneg` is ADMITTED even though LLVM groups it with FP arithmetic, and
# `bitcast i32 -> float` is ADMITTED while `sitofp i32 -> float` is REJECTED.
# Those two are the non-obvious placements and both are pinned below.
#
# WHAT THIS TEST CHECKS: that a hand-authored module can be built entirely from
# the admitted surface and survive assemble/verify/disassemble under LLVM
# 17.0.6, and that each rejected opcode class is detected by the harness gate
# with the correct harness expectation string.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT CHECK: NFConforms, any ModelStatus, DeploymentStatus, or
# PolicyReviewStatus; the transition-rule audit; the actual
# NoAmbiguousNaNResult_e(T) gate. tools/nf_surface_gate.py is a syntactic
# opcode scanner, and the reason-class strings it prints are harness
# EXPECTATION records for a future Rev4 run, never computed results. The
# normative boundary is LLVM 22.1.8, which does not exist on this machine.

# ===========================================================================
# ACCEPTED ARM -- the admitted surface assembles, verifies, and round-trips
# ===========================================================================
# RUN: %llvm-as %harness/integration/Inputs/sps-rev4-nf/a02-scalar-fp-admitted.ll.in -o %t.admitted.bc
# RUN: %opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.admitted.bc
# RUN: %llvm-dis %t.admitted.bc -o %t.admitted.ll

# The integer half: flag-free modulo arithmetic with checked div/shift
# operands. `udiv`/`urem` take a divisor that is provably nonzero on this path
# and `shl`/`lshr` take an amount masked below the operand width, which is the
# "checked division and shift operands" NF-A02 names.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-INT --input-file=%t.admitted.ll
# A02-INT-LABEL: define i32 @a02_checked_integer_surface(i32 %a, i32 %b, i32 %shift)
# A02-INT: %sum = add i32 %a, %b
# A02-INT: %checked_divisor = select i1 %divisor_is_zero, i32 1, i32 %b
# A02-INT: %quotient = udiv i32 %prod, %checked_divisor
# A02-INT: %checked_amount = and i32 %shift, 31
# A02-INT: %shifted = shl i32 %quotient, %checked_amount

# No `nsw`/`nuw`/`exact` flag survives anywhere in the module: NF-A02 says
# flag-free. Non-vacuous because the mutation arm at the bottom shows the same
# grep firing once a single opcode changes.
# RUN: not grep -qE '\b(nsw|nuw|exact)\b' %t.admitted.ll

# The FP half, pinned as counts rather than presence.
# RUN: grep -cE '^  %[^ ]+ = fneg ' %t.admitted.ll | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-FNEG-COUNT
# A02-FNEG-COUNT: 2
# RUN: grep -cE '^  %[^ ]+ = fcmp ' %t.admitted.ll | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-FCMP-COUNT
# A02-FCMP-COUNT: 2
# RUN: grep -cE '^  %[^ ]+ = bitcast ' %t.admitted.ll | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-BITCAST-COUNT
# A02-BITCAST-COUNT: 3

# Same-width bitcasts in both directions, which is the pair that makes the
# sitofp arm below meaningful: identical operand and result types, different
# admissibility.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-BITCAST --input-file=%t.admitted.ll
# A02-BITCAST: %bits = bitcast double %merged to i64
# A02-BITCAST: %as_float = bitcast i32 %encoded to float
# A02-BITCAST: %back = bitcast float %selected to i32

# The gate agrees, and exits 0. `rejected-fp-items:` is immediately followed by
# the summary line, so the rejected list is pinned EMPTY by adjacency rather
# than by a CHECK-NOT that could pass vacuously.
# RUN: %python %harness/tools/nf_surface_gate.py --profile fp-closure %t.admitted.ll | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-ADMIT
# A02-ADMIT: SPS-Harness-Surface-Gate-v1
# A02-ADMIT: profile: fp-closure
# A02-ADMIT: admitted-bit-preserving-fp-items:
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: load 1
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: store 1
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: bitcast 3
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: phi 1
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: select 2
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: fneg 2
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: fcmp 2
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: rejected-fp-items:
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: summary: rejected-fp-item-count=0
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: SPS-Harness-Expectation: NF-A02 rejected-FP surface is textually empty in this module; the NoAmbiguousNaNResult_e(T) gate is NOT thereby established
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: SPS-Harness-Boundary: tier=PreflightV1 nf_conforms=NotEvaluated model_status=NotComputed deployment_status=NotComputed
# A02-ADMIT-NEXT: SPS-Harness-Note: syntactic opcode/type scan of one textual module under LLVM 17.0.6; not the Rev4 normal-form audit and not a proof

# ===========================================================================
# REJECTED ARM 1 -- FP arithmetic (`fadd`)
# ===========================================================================
# RUN: %llvm-as %harness/integration/Inputs/sps-rev4-nf/a02-rejected-fadd.ll.in -o %t.fadd.bc
# RUN: %opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.fadd.bc
# RUN: %llvm-dis %t.fadd.bc -o %t.fadd.ll
# RUN: not %python %harness/tools/nf_surface_gate.py --profile fp-closure %t.fadd.ll 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-FADD
# A02-FADD: rejected-fp-items:
# A02-FADD-NEXT: line {{[0-9]+}} in @a02_fp_arithmetic: fadd (fp-arithmetic): %sum = fadd double %left, %right
# The second hit is behind `br i1 false`. R5.0N refuses it anyway: rejection is
# syntactic, "even if it is dynamically unreachable".
# A02-FADD-NEXT: line {{[0-9]+}} in @unreachable_fadd: fadd (fp-arithmetic): %sum = fadd double %left, %right
# A02-FADD-NEXT: summary: rejected-fp-item-count=2
# A02-FADD-NEXT: SPS-Harness-Expectation: Unknown(PONFFPArithmeticUnsupported) -- NF-A02 admits no residual FP arithmetic, FP-width conversion, or FP/integer numeric conversion (Lemma R5.0N)
# A02-FADD: SPS-Harness-Boundary: tier=PreflightV1 nf_conforms=NotEvaluated model_status=NotComputed deployment_status=NotComputed

# The dead branch really is still in the module the gate scanned; the arm would
# be trivial if llvm-as had folded it away.
# RUN: grep -q 'br i1 false' %t.fadd.ll

# ===========================================================================
# REJECTED ARM 2 -- FP-width conversion (`fptrunc`, and its `fpext` partner)
# ===========================================================================
# RUN: %llvm-as %harness/integration/Inputs/sps-rev4-nf/a02-rejected-fptrunc.ll.in -o %t.fptrunc.bc
# RUN: %opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.fptrunc.bc
# RUN: %llvm-dis %t.fptrunc.bc -o %t.fptrunc.ll
# RUN: not %python %harness/tools/nf_surface_gate.py --profile fp-closure %t.fptrunc.ll 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-FPTRUNC
# A02-FPTRUNC: rejected-fp-items:
# A02-FPTRUNC-NEXT: line {{[0-9]+}} in @a02_fp_width_narrowing: fptrunc (fp-width-conversion): %narrow = fptrunc double %wide to float
# A02-FPTRUNC-NEXT: line {{[0-9]+}} in @a02_fp_width_widening: fpext (fp-width-conversion): %wide = fpext float %narrow to double
# A02-FPTRUNC-NEXT: summary: rejected-fp-item-count=2
# A02-FPTRUNC-NEXT: SPS-Harness-Expectation: Unknown(PONFFPArithmeticUnsupported)

# ===========================================================================
# REJECTED ARM 3 -- FP/integer NUMERIC conversion (`sitofp` and friends)
# ===========================================================================
# This is the arm that separates "mentions a float type" from "renumbers the
# value". `bitcast i32 -> float` is admitted above; `sitofp i32 -> float` has
# the same operand and result types and is rejected.
# RUN: %llvm-as %harness/integration/Inputs/sps-rev4-nf/a02-rejected-sitofp.ll.in -o %t.sitofp.bc
# RUN: %opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.sitofp.bc
# RUN: %llvm-dis %t.sitofp.bc -o %t.sitofp.ll
# RUN: not %python %harness/tools/nf_surface_gate.py --profile fp-closure %t.sitofp.ll 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-SITOFP
# A02-SITOFP: rejected-fp-items:
# A02-SITOFP-NEXT: line {{[0-9]+}} in @a02_signed_integer_to_fp: sitofp (fp-integer-numeric-conversion): %converted = sitofp i32 %value to float
# A02-SITOFP-NEXT: line {{[0-9]+}} in @a02_fp_to_signed_integer: fptosi (fp-integer-numeric-conversion): %converted = fptosi float %value to i32
# A02-SITOFP-NEXT: line {{[0-9]+}} in @a02_unsigned_integer_to_fp: uitofp (fp-integer-numeric-conversion): %converted = uitofp i64 %value to double
# A02-SITOFP-NEXT: summary: rejected-fp-item-count=3
# A02-SITOFP-NEXT: SPS-Harness-Expectation: Unknown(PONFFPArithmeticUnsupported)

# ===========================================================================
# DISCRIMINATION ARM -- one opcode substitution flips the accepted module
# ===========================================================================
# The accepted arm's `not grep` and `rejected-fp-item-count=0` would both pass
# on any module with no FP at all. This arm removes that doubt: take the
# ACCEPTED module, replace exactly one admitted `fneg` with a rejected `fmul`,
# change nothing else, and watch both mechanisms fire.
# RUN: sed 's/fneg double %value/fmul double %value, %value/' %harness/integration/Inputs/sps-rev4-nf/a02-scalar-fp-admitted.ll.in > %t.mutated.ll.in
# RUN: not cmp -s %t.mutated.ll.in %harness/integration/Inputs/sps-rev4-nf/a02-scalar-fp-admitted.ll.in
# RUN: %llvm-as %t.mutated.ll.in -o %t.mutated.bc
# RUN: %opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.mutated.bc
# RUN: %llvm-dis %t.mutated.bc -o %t.mutated.ll

# The raw grep that was silent on the accepted module now has exactly one hit.
# RUN: grep -cE '^  %[^ ]+ = (fadd|fsub|fmul|fdiv|frem|fptrunc|fpext|fptosi|fptoui|sitofp|uitofp) ' %t.mutated.ll | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-MUTATED-COUNT
# A02-MUTATED-COUNT: 1

# And the gate flips from exit 0 to exit 1, with `fneg` down from 2 to 1.
# RUN: not %python %harness/tools/nf_surface_gate.py --profile fp-closure %t.mutated.ll 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A02-MUTATED
# A02-MUTATED: fneg 1
# A02-MUTATED: rejected-fp-items:
# A02-MUTATED-NEXT: line {{[0-9]+}} in @a02_double_bit_preserving: fmul (fp-arithmetic): %negated = fmul double %value, %value
# A02-MUTATED-NEXT: summary: rejected-fp-item-count=1
# A02-MUTATED-NEXT: SPS-Harness-Expectation: Unknown(PONFFPArithmeticUnsupported)

# INTERPRETATION.
#
# A green run here means: the admitted NF-A02 surface is expressible and stable
# under LLVM 17.0.6 assemble/verify/disassemble, and each of the three rejected
# classes is separated from it by a syntactic scan whose recorded expectation is
# Unknown(PONFFPArithmeticUnsupported).
#
# It does not mean NoAmbiguousNaNResult_e(T) holds for any artifact. That gate
# is over the FROZEN CLOSURE of a canonical LLVM 22.1.8 module -- including
# everything reachable through calls and intrinsics -- and this scan reads one
# textual file with no call-graph closure and no identity binding. A module
# that passes this test can still fail the real gate through a callee.
